    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ENP102 · Assessment 1/4</span>\n<h2>Assignment(s)</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13844 · assessment table (verbatim)</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ENP102 · Đầu điểm 1/4</span>\n<h2>Assignment(s)</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13844 · bảng đánh giá (nguyên văn)</p></div>\n<div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type / Loại</span><span class=\"v\">on-going</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Weight / Trọng số</span><span class=\"v\">30.0%</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Parts / Số phần</span><span class=\"v\">1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Completion criteria / Điều kiện hoàn thành</span><span class=\"v\">&gt;0</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">CLO</span><span class=\"v\">LO1, LO2 , LO4, LO5, LO6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Question type / Dạng câu hỏi</span><span class=\"v\">Teachers can flexibly choose different formats for students to complete the assignment. Here are some suggestions for teachers to choose:Suggestion 1: Students record speakers who have mispronunciations (they can be students from outside the class or students within the class) and use those recordings as the main material for creating the pronunciation guide. Those short clips should only be used as practice examples or for comparison with the mispronounced samples. The content should focus only on analyzing consonant and vowel sounds.Students analyze the clip focusing only on the content they have learned:A. Consonant Sounds· Identify and list examples of consonants in the clip that are commonly difficult for Vietnamese learners (e.g., /θ/, /ð/, /ʃ/, /tʃ/, /ʒ/, /v/, /z/, final stops /p t k/, etc.).· Provide short IPA transcriptions only for word-level items, not full sentences.· Identify misleading spellings (e.g., “knife” /naɪf/)B. Vowel Sounds· Identify key vowel sounds in the clip that differ significantly from Vietnamese vowels.· Provide minimal IPA transcription of sample words (e.g., ship vs sheep, cup vs calf).· Comment briefly on vowel length contrasts or tense vs. lax vowel differences, if applicable.No analysis of diphthongs, triphthongs, stress, linking, rhythm, or intonation.Group Collaboration:Work in teams of 3–4 to compile findings and present them in a short video or slide presentation.Suggestion 2:Students work in pairs and make a dialogue in which they should use the following aspects of sounds (the same as Speaking part 1 in FE)- Vowels- Consonants- Dipthongs- Elision- Linking consonant sounds to vowel sounds- Intrusion- Assimilation</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">No. of questions / Số câu</span><span class=\"v\">Flexible</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Knowledge &amp; skill / Kiến thức &amp; kỹ năng</span><span class=\"v\">Based on topics of studied units</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Grading guide / Hướng dẫn chấm</span><span class=\"v\">Flexible</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Note / Ghi chú</span><span class=\"v\">The date of the assignment is decided by the teacher.</span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><p class=\"ghi-chu\">No practice paper for this subject in the Exam Room yet.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><p class=\"ghi-chu\">Phòng thi chưa có đề luyện cho môn này.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Exam-strategy notes and worked past papers: coming later.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Chiến lược làm bài và chữa đề: sẽ bổ sung sau.</div></div>"
